  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "8268530",
      "title": "Adding Question Timers",
      "sourceHash": "adb4588de22831e5d09ed6c7014ae71105086fc2646729006d19e04b26250119",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.48,
          "end": 2.94,
          "en": "So now that this quiz is slowly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.94,
          "end": 5.13,
          "en": "but steadily taking shape,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.13,
          "end": 8.37,
          "en": "before we'll work on this game over screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.37,
          "end": 11.16,
          "en": "where I of course also wanna tell the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.16,
          "end": 14.76,
          "en": "how many questions were answered correctly and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.76,
          "end": 19.76,
          "en": "Before we do that, I wanna add an extra feature to this quiz",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.98,
          "end": 23.46,
          "en": "because I wanna make sure that for every question,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.46,
          "end": 27.21,
          "en": "you have a limited amount of time to answer it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.21,
          "end": 31.89,
          "en": "Let's say 15 seconds or something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.89,
          "end": 34.8,
          "en": "And I wanna have a little progress bar",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.8,
          "end": 39.54,
          "en": "that's slowly depleting as this timer expires.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.54,
          "end": 41.64,
          "en": "And if the timer did expire,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.64,
          "end": 44.22,
          "en": "the next question should be presented",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.22,
          "end": 47.22,
          "en": "and this question should be skipped.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.22,
          "end": 50.1,
          "en": "So if the user does not answer in time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.1,
          "end": 52.503,
          "en": "no answer will be registered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.97,
          "end": 57.903,
          "en": "And to implement this, we will now use useEffect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.86,
          "end": 60.51,
          "en": "But of course, as you can tell,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.51,
          "end": 63.87,
          "en": "this quiz component is already growing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.87,
          "end": 66.12,
          "en": "in complexity and size,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.12,
          "end": 69.42,
          "en": "and therefore I'll outsource this timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.42,
          "end": 72.21000000000001,
          "en": "into a brand new component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.21000000000001,
          "end": 75.39,
          "en": "I'll add a question timer component file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.39,
          "end": 77.67,
          "en": "called QuestionTimer.jsx.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.67,
          "end": 79.83,
          "en": "And in that file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.83,
          "end": 84.39,
          "en": "I wanna export a new component function QuestionTimer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.52,
          "end": 89.78999999999999,
          "en": "And here the goal in this file then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.78999999999999,
          "end": 93.72,
          "en": "is to display this progress bar,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.72,
          "end": 96.87,
          "en": "so the default progress element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.87,
          "end": 99.18,
          "en": "But of course, this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.18,
          "end": 102.81,
          "en": "will not just be about displaying this progress bar,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.81,
          "end": 106.86,
          "en": "it will also be about managing this progress bar.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.86,
          "end": 108.12,
          "en": "Now, I will actually start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.12,
          "end": 110.97,
          "en": "by giving this an id, question time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.97,
          "end": 113.553,
          "en": "which is there for styling purposes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.78,
          "end": 116.75999999999999,
          "en": "But then to add some logic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.75999999999999,
          "end": 121.76,
          "en": "we also wanna set a timer that expires after sometime,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.13,
          "end": 126.15,
          "en": "and we can do that with the built-in setTimeout function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 126.15,
          "end": 128.4,
          "en": "as you learned before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.4,
          "end": 129.75,
          "en": "We then just have to define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.75,
          "end": 132.57,
          "en": "after how much time this should expire.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.57,
          "end": 136.05,
          "en": "And here, I think it would be great if this question timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.05,
          "end": 139.02,
          "en": "would be a configurable component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 139.02,
          "end": 143.79,
          "en": "so that the exact time is not hard coded in this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 143.79,
          "end": 146.13,
          "en": "but can be defined in the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.13,
          "end": 149.733,
          "en": "where this question timer component is being used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.6,
          "end": 153.81,
          "en": "Hence, I'll destructure my props object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.81,
          "end": 156.84,
          "en": "and I expect to get a timeout prop here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 156.84,
          "end": 160.173,
          "en": "which is the timeout that should be set on this timer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 161.52,
          "end": 163.26,
          "en": "So that could then, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 163.26,
          "end": 167.253,
          "en": "be 15,000 milliseconds, so 15 seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 168.21,
          "end": 170.91,
          "en": "Then once the timer expired,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.91,
          "end": 175.07999999999998,
          "en": "I wanna let the parent component know about that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 175.07999999999998,
          "end": 179.16,
          "en": "So that if we use question timer in the quiz component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 179.16,
          "end": 181.5,
          "en": "we actually are notified",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 181.5,
          "end": 184.92,
          "en": "that we should move on to the next question,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.92,
          "end": 186.99,
          "en": "because it's this quiz component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 186.99,
          "end": 190.74,
          "en": "where I'm managing the active question.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 190.74,
          "end": 195.09,
          "en": "Therefore, question timer also should receive another prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 195.09,
          "end": 197.64,
          "en": "that should be a function that should be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 197.64,
          "end": 201.18,
          "en": "from inside this timer once it expired,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 201.18,
          "end": 205.14,
          "en": "and that could be onTimeout, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 205.14,
          "end": 209.667,
          "en": "So that in here, in this timer, I call onTimeout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 210.66,
          "end": 214.77,
          "en": "And we can actually shorten this code and just set onTimeout",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 214.77,
          "end": 217.74,
          "en": "as the function that should be called by the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 217.74,
          "end": 219.543,
          "en": "once this timeout expired.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 221.1,
          "end": 224.88,
          "en": "Now, I'm not using useEffect here at this point",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 224.88,
          "end": 227.57999999999998,
          "en": "because even though this is a side effect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 227.57999999999998,
          "end": 229.8,
          "en": "it's at the moment not an effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 229.8,
          "end": 232.65,
          "en": "that would require the usage of useEffect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 232.65,
          "end": 236.55,
          "en": "because I'm not facing the danger of an infinite loop here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 236.55,
          "end": 240.03,
          "en": "because I'm not updating any component state here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 240.03,
          "end": 243.57,
          "en": "and I'm also not trying to interact with an element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 243.57,
          "end": 245.94,
          "en": "that wouldn't be available yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 245.94,
          "end": 249.933,
          "en": "So this code at the moment is fine as it is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 251.82,
          "end": 254.73,
          "en": "but of course that's not all I wanna do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 254.73,
          "end": 257.46,
          "en": "Instead, I also wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 257.46,
          "end": 260.64,
          "en": "that I update this progress bar,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 260.64,
          "end": 263.25,
          "en": "and therefore we also need an interval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 263.25,
          "end": 267.18,
          "en": "that executes some code every couple of milliseconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 267.18,
          "end": 269.673,
          "en": "so that we can update this timer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 270.69,
          "end": 272.58,
          "en": "Therefore, we of course also need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 272.58,
          "end": 276.09000000000003,
          "en": "some state in this component so that this progress bar",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 276.09000000000003,
          "end": 279,
          "en": "is rerendered every couple of milliseconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 279,
          "end": 280.743,
          "en": "whenever that state changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 281.88,
          "end": 286.78,
          "en": "So I'll import useState from React here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 287.7,
          "end": 291.27,
          "en": "and then the state that is registered here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 291.27,
          "end": 294.75,
          "en": "is in the end the remaining time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 294.75,
          "end": 296.65,
          "en": "so remainingTime and setRemainingTime.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 300.54,
          "end": 304.86,
          "en": "The initial value for the state should be this timeout value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 304.86,
          "end": 308.61,
          "en": "because that is the remaining time of this timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 308.61,
          "end": 310.533,
          "en": "when this component is rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 312.54,
          "end": 316.41,
          "en": "But then I wanna update this every 10 milliseconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 316.41,
          "end": 318.06,
          "en": "or something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 318.06,
          "end": 322.443,
          "en": "And therefore we of course need set interval as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 323.43,
          "end": 325.14,
          "en": "because here we can define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 325.14,
          "end": 329.58,
          "en": "that every 10 or 100 or whatever milliseconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 329.58,
          "end": 332.19,
          "en": "this function here should execute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 332.19,
          "end": 335.88,
          "en": "And in this function, I wanna update my remaining time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 335.88,
          "end": 338.85,
          "en": "by deducting 100 milliseconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 338.85,
          "end": 342.33299999999997,
          "en": "or whichever frequency you chose here from it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 343.771,
          "end": 347.55,
          "en": "So here we need the function form since we update the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 347.55,
          "end": 351.123,
          "en": "based on the previously stored state value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 351.99,
          "end": 355.5,
          "en": "And the new value is standard previously remaining time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 355.5,
          "end": 359.223,
          "en": "minus 100, so minus my frequency here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 361.74,
          "end": 365.76,
          "en": "And this would now of course create an infinite loop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 365.76,
          "end": 367.8,
          "en": "because we're updating the state here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 367.8,
          "end": 371.31,
          "en": "This would re-execute this component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 371.31,
          "end": 373.23,
          "en": "We would create a new interval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 373.23,
          "end": 375.66,
          "en": "where we would also update the state again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 375.66,
          "end": 379.14,
          "en": "and we would quickly have multiple intervals up and running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 379.14,
          "end": 383.01,
          "en": "which all would call this component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 383.01,
          "end": 385.86,
          "en": "And that's of course definitely not what we want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 385.86,
          "end": 389.47,
          "en": "and that's therefore a use case for useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 390.96,
          "end": 395.17,
          "en": "because now we can wrap this code with useEffect here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 396.6,
          "end": 399.48,
          "en": "by passing this effect function to useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 399.48,
          "end": 402.39300000000003,
          "en": "and this dependencies array about which you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 404.88,
          "end": 408.12,
          "en": "And then we should move this set interval code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 408.12,
          "end": 411.24,
          "en": "into useEffect to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 411.24,
          "end": 414.18,
          "en": "that this is not re executed all the time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 414.18,
          "end": 417.663,
          "en": "but instead only when those dependencies change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 418.62,
          "end": 421.92,
          "en": "And in here, we don't have any dependencies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 421.92,
          "end": 423.99,
          "en": "that would need to be added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 423.99,
          "end": 426.57,
          "en": "because you basically only need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 426.57,
          "end": 429.24,
          "en": "to add props and state values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 429.24,
          "end": 432.963,
          "en": "and we're using neither of those in this effect function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 435.03,
          "end": 437.4,
          "en": "But we should now of course also wrap",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 437.4,
          "end": 439.92,
          "en": "this timeout code with useEffect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 439.92,
          "end": 443.64,
          "en": "because otherwise when we update the remaining time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 443.64,
          "end": 446.58,
          "en": "which we will do every 100 milliseconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 446.58,
          "end": 448.95,
          "en": "this component function executes again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 448.95,
          "end": 452.19,
          "en": "and this timer would be recreated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 452.19,
          "end": 454.02,
          "en": "and we therefore would quickly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 454.02,
          "end": 456.423,
          "en": "have multiple timers up and running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 457.86,
          "end": 461.5,
          "en": "Therefore, we should add another useEffect call here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 463.05,
